# Example environment variables for the OctoFit frontend
# The REACT_APP_CODESPACE_NAME value will be auto-populated from the runtime CODESPACE_NAME
# when you run the npm scripts in this project (see package.json). If you prefer to set it
# explicitly during development, copy this file to `.env` and change the value below.
#
# To rely on the Codespace value (recommended in Codespaces): leave this file as-is and
# ensure the `CODESPACE_NAME` environment variable exists in your environment.
#
# To set it manually for local development, copy to `.env` and set:
# REACT_APP_CODESPACE_NAME=your-codespace-name

REACT_APP_CODESPACE_NAME=your-codespace-name
